  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Plugin Subscriptions",
      "text": "AI LLM plugin for DeepSeek Harness that signs in to consumer AI subscriptions with OAuth and exposes them as LLM providers."
    },
    {
      "section": "Live",
      "text": "| Provider | Subscription | Notes |\n|----------|-------------|-------|\n| **Claude** | Anthropic Pro/Max | Imports credentials from Claude Code automatically; run `claude` first |\n| **Codex** | ChatGPT Plus/Pro | Real-time model discovery from `chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex/models` |\n| **Grok** | X Premium/Premium+ | Real-time model discovery; includes `x_search`, `image_generate`, `video_generate` tools |\n| **Google Antigravity** | Google One AI Premium | 静态目录（Gemini 3 Pro / 3.1 Pro / 3 Flash, Claude 4.6 Sonnet / Opus）；直接 OAuth，无需环境变量 |\n| **OpenRouter** | OpenRouter account | OAuth PKCE → permanent API key; static catalog (GPT-4o, Claude Sonnet/Haiku 4.5, Gemini 2.5 Flash) |\n| **Agnes AI** | AgnesCode account | OAuth PKCE → access token (reverse-engineered); static catalog (Agnes 2.5/2.0 Flash, GPT-4o, Claude Sonnet 4.5 via AgnesCode) |\n| **Qwen Code** | Qwen Coding Plan | Device-flow OAuth via `chat.qwen.ai`；无需 API Key |\n| **iFlytek Spark** | Spark API subscription | OAuth PKCE via `spark-api.xf-yun.com`; env vars: `SPARK_CLIENT_ID`, `SPARK_CLIENT_SECRET` |\n| **Baidu ERNIE** | ERNIE Bot subscription | OAuth PKCE via `openapi.baidu.com`; env vars: `ERNIE_CLIENT_ID`, `ERNIE_CLIENT_S"
    },
    {
      "section": "Coming soon",
      "text": "Gemini, Perplexity AI, GitHub Copilot, Mistral AI, Cursor, Hugging Face, Windsurf, Replicate, fal.ai, Cohere, Voyage AI, Lepton AI, OctoAI."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- OAuth sign-in for subscription providers — no API keys required\n- Composer model resolution straight from your subscription\n- Streaming, tool calling, and image input where the provider supports them\n- Usage status shown in the Subscriptions settings section\n- Built-in model catalogs per provider, overridable in config"
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "From npm (pre-built, no build step)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-plugin-subs"
    },
    {
      "section": "Or from GitHub source",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add github:randomix777/dsh-plugin-subs\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "1. Launch DSH (`dsh web`) and open the printed URL.\n2. Go to **Settings → Subscriptions** and press **Connect** next to a provider.\n3. Complete the OAuth flow in the browser tab that opens. On headless setups, paste the callback URL or authorization code manually.\n   - **Claude**: imports from existing Claude Code credentials (run `claude` once if not logged in).\n    - **Antigravity**: no env vars needed, complete OAuth in browser directly; optionally override with `ANTIGRAVITY_CLIENT_ID` / `ANTIGRAVITY_CLIENT_SECRET`.\n    - **Qwen Code**: device-flow OAuth via `chat.qwen.ai`; no API key or env vars required, click Connect to authenticate.\n    - **Agnes AI**: after browser authorization, paste the full callback URL (or just the auth code) into the DSH UI — the `agnes://` deep link cannot be auto-captured by DSH.\n4. In any chat, open the model selector (`/model`) and pick a model under the desired provider."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Untreated providers show no card in the model picker until signed in."
    },
    {
      "section": "Environment Variables",
      "text": "Antigravity and Qwen use embedded public client credentials — no setup required. Only Spark and ERNIE need env vars:\n\n```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Optional: override the built-in Antigravity OAuth client credentials",
      "text": "export ANTIGRAVITY_CLIENT_ID=\"your-custom-oauth-client-id\"\nexport ANTIGRAVITY_CLIENT_SECRET=\"your-custom-oauth-client-secret\""
    },
    {
      "section": "iFlytek Spark (register at https://console.xfyun.cn)",
      "text": "export SPARK_CLIENT_ID=\"your-spark-client-id\"\nexport SPARK_CLIENT_SECRET=\"your-spark-client-secret\""
    },
    {
      "section": "Baidu ERNIE (register at https://console.bce.baidu.com/ai/)",
      "text": "export ERNIE_CLIENT_ID=\"your-ernie-client-id\"\nexport ERNIE_CLIENT_SECRET=\"your-ernie-client-secret\"\n```\n\nSpark and ERNIE require you to register an OAuth app on the respective platform and set the env vars above."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "```yaml\nproviders:\n  - id: llm-subscriptions\n    name: dsh-plugin-subs\n    config:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "Auto-registered when the corresponding provider is active:\n\n- **`x_search`** (Grok) — xAI-hosted X search, returns `{ answer, citations }`\n- **`image_generate`** (Codex or Grok) — calls `gpt-image-2` via Codex backend or `grok-imagine-image-2.0` via Grok; saves to `~/.dsh/plugins/subscriptions/images/`\n- **`video_generate`** (Grok) — calls `grok-imagine-video-1.5` via `api.x.ai/v1/videos`; async poll, saves MP4 to `~/.dsh/plugins/subscriptions/videos/`"
    },
    {
      "section": "Limitations",
      "text": "- Provider availability depends on your subscription status; unsigned-in providers are hidden\n- Image generation requires an active Codex or Grok session\n- `x_search` requires Grok login and an API-capable subscription tier\n- OpenRouter API key is permanent (no refresh); log out and re-login to replace\n- Agnes AI requires manual callback URL/code paste (no `agnes://` protocol handler in DSH)\n- Chinese providers (Spark, ERNIE) require a registered OAuth app on the respective platform and env var credentials\n- Qwen Code uses device-flow OAuth: enter the user code at the verification URL in any browser; the flow is cancellable and expires after `expires_in` seconds"
    },
    {
      "section": "Project Structure",
      "text": "- `lib/index.js` — Main bundle (compiled output), all backend logic\n- `lib/client.js` — Browser bundle, UI components\n- `lib/client/*.js` — Split client source files (locales, UI components)"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
